.IX Title "Lucy::Index::SegWriter 3pm"
.TH Lucy::Index::SegWriter 3pm 2026-09-16 "perl v5.40.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
Lucy::Index::SegWriter \- Write one segment of an index.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
SegWriter is a conduit through which information fed to Indexer passes.  It
manages Segment and Inverter, invokes the
Analyzer chain, and feeds low
level DataWriters such as
PostingListWriter and DocWriter.
.PP
The sub-components of a SegWriter are determined by
Architecture.  DataWriter components
which are added to the stack of writers via \fBadd_writer()\fR have
\&\fBAdd_Inverted_Doc()\fR invoked for each document supplied to SegWriter’s
\&\fBadd_doc()\fR.
.SH METHODS
.IX Header "METHODS"
.SS register
.IX Subsection "register"
.Vb 4
\&    $seg_writer\->register(
\&        api       => $api,        # required
\&        component => $component,  # required
\&    );
.Ve
.PP
Register a DataWriter component with the SegWriter.  (Note that
registration simply makes the writer available via \fBfetch()\fR, so you may
also want to call \fBadd_writer()\fR).
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBapi\fR \- The name of the DataWriter api which \f(CW\*(C`writer\*(C'\fR
implements.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBcomponent\fR \- A DataWriter.
.SS fetch
.IX Subsection "fetch"
.Vb 1
\&    my $obj = $seg_writer\->fetch($api);
.Ve
.PP
Retrieve a registered component.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBapi\fR \- The name of the DataWriter api which the component
implements.
.SS add_writer
.IX Subsection "add_writer"
.Vb 1
\&    $seg_writer\->add_writer($writer);
.Ve
.PP
Add a DataWriter to the SegWriter’s stack of writers.
.SS add_doc
.IX Subsection "add_doc"
.Vb 4
\&    $seg_writer\->add_doc(
\&        doc   => $doc,    # required
\&        boost => $boost,  # default: 1.0
\&    );
.Ve
.PP
Add a document to the segment.  Inverts \f(CW\*(C`doc\*(C'\fR, increments
the Segment’s internal document id, then calls \fBAdd_Inverted_Doc()\fR,
feeding all sub-writers.
.SS add_segment
.IX Subsection "add_segment"
.Vb 4
\&    $seg_writer\->add_segment(
\&        reader  => $reader,   # required
\&        doc_map => $doc_map,  # default: undef
\&    );
.Ve
.PP
Add content from an existing segment into the one currently being
written.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBreader\fR \- The SegReader containing content to add.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBdoc_map\fR \- An array of integers mapping old document ids to
new.  Deleted documents are mapped to 0, indicating that they should be
skipped.
.SS finish
.IX Subsection "finish"
.Vb 1
\&    $seg_writer\->finish();
.Ve
.PP
Complete the segment: close all streams, store metadata, etc.
.SH INHERITANCE
.IX Header "INHERITANCE"
Lucy::Index::SegWriter isa Lucy::Index::DataWriter isa Clownfish::Obj.
